// The spell checker's dictionary. Generated — do NOT hand-edit the blob below.
//
// LOADED ON DEMAND. utils/spellSuggest.js pulls this in with a dynamic
// import(), so it becomes its own chunk and does not sit in the main bundle
// that every page pays for. Only a screen with a comment box on it ever
// downloads it, and only once.
//
// TWO SECTIONS, AND THE ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING:
//
//   1. HEAD — the ~10,000 most frequent English words, in frequency order,
//      followed by this module's own vocabulary (syllabus, accreditation, the
//      CS course names, the words that turn up in approver comments, and
//      enough Filipino and Filipino surnames that Taglish is not underlined).
//   2. TAIL — the rest of a 32,000-word frequency list, alphabetical.
//
// `suggest()` ranks candidates by their index here, so head words — the common
// ones — are always offered before tail words. That is the whole reason the
// head is not sorted with everything else: sorting compresses better, but it
// would rank "abaci" above "about".
//
// Every entry is intersected with a full English word list before it lands
// here, so a frequency corpus's own misspellings cannot get in and be treated
// as correct. (Two do survive — "wich" and "untill" — and both are in
// reviewGate's MISSPELLINGS, which overrides this file.)

